This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

It is a MUTATION BATTERY. Seven of its arms build copies of core's own
reconcile/ directory, restore one site's pre-fix process-substitution spelling in
ledger-reverify.sh, preclassify.sh, emit-report.sh or self-update-gate.sh, and prove the forced
arm that watches the site reads that site's old false verdict again. Those four scripts are
installed and a consumer cannot edit them in place (ai-dlc-core-guard.sh), so on a consumer the
battery would only re-derive an answer about this repository's sources.

The forced arms beside the mutants use synthetic worlds and would run on a consumer. They are
kept beside their mutants rather than split into a shipping sibling because each mutant is
scored on the forced arm's own shape and nothing else. A shipping copy of the forced arms alone
would be a second copy of the stubs and the shape table with nothing binding the two.
